translate english d5_ending_past_f8651883:


    "We continued on our way, with just the two of us."


translate english d5_ending_past_35d787ca:


    "The blizzard howled, and we ran, our breathing ragged."


translate english d5_ending_past_2c1b8b5f:


    "Rifle fire echoed over the burial grounds."


translate english d5_ending_past_9f5b6474:


    "Polina fell down, and I helped her up."


translate english d5_ending_past_7ca76651:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/226 g.ogg" 
    Pol "Where is he?"


translate english d5_ending_past_58ef80e5:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/213.On.ogg" 
    Ant "He'd want us to save ourselves. That's the most important part."


translate english d5_ending_past_53831a63:


    "The rifle rattled off in the night, spewing lead."


translate english d5_ending_past_d67f7f45:


    "And then it suddenly went silent, and the howling blizzard subsided in unison."


translate english d5_ending_past_90a9bb84:


    "The snowy blanket slowly covered the graves, opening up the gray sky and the bright moon."


translate english d5_ending_past_3357e447:


    "Its light illuminated the gravestones, the dead people on oval-shaped photos, and Polina's and my faces."


translate english d5_ending_past_397e0a8a:


    "Did Tikhonov run out of ammo?"


translate english d5_ending_past_faf743ae:


    "Or did his life end? There, in the snowstorm, after being torn to pieces..."


translate english d5_ending_past_c4f3ecdc:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/214.Scor.ogg"
    Ant "Come on, let's go."


translate english d5_ending_past_303f26f6:


    "We walked like two lost kids."


translate english d5_ending_past_26919279:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/227 sl.ogg" 
    Pol "Hear that?"


translate english d5_ending_past_63c9f07c:


    "I strained my hearing."


translate english d5_ending_past_3489fe03:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/214.no.ogg"
    Ant "N-no."


translate english d5_ending_past_a47929cc:


    "She stopped me with a gesture, listening intently to the grave silence around us."


translate english d5_ending_past_5e8307b1:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/01 ab.ogg"
    Pol "Complete silence. I can't hear any music."


translate english d5_ending_past_4dd42a87:


    "And then she cried."


translate english d5_ending_past_c50e0939:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/03 me.ogg"
    Pol "The melodies of Olya... Tikhonov... Romka..."


translate english d5_ending_past_d8f967cc:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/04 eh.ogg"
    Pol "They're gone."


translate english d5_ending_past_f707d14c:


    "Her words made me burn up."


translate english d5_ending_past_9beb885c:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/215.Poz.ogg"
    Ant "Please, Polina, you saw what those monsters can do!"


translate english d5_ending_past_a4b5759f:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/215.Pro.ogg"
    Ant "Come on, we need to go!"


translate english d5_ending_past_beea634e:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/05 be.ogg"
    Pol "Without Olya? Without Romka?"


translate english d5_ending_past_72bd01cb:


    "She wailed, and bitter tears appeared in the corner of my eyes, too."


translate english d5_ending_past_5f91a0e9:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/216.Slez.ogg"
    Ant "We can't bring them back with tears."


translate english d5_ending_past_cef5fc7a:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/216.no.ogg"
    Ant "But I promise I'll save you."


translate english d5_ending_past_c021449d:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/217.E.ogg"
    Ant "And we'll definitely go to Moscow, to Vienna, and I..."


translate english d5_ending_past_b8a9c891:


    "She sniffled and stared at me."


translate english d5_ending_past_9d6f2516:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/218.Ya.ogg"
    Ant "...I'll publish my comic book about you, Polina."


translate english d5_ending_past_1f16d7c9:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/219.Ver.ogg"
    Ant "Believe me!"


translate english d5_ending_past_3c9e40c6:


    "Polina hugged me as she whispered:"


translate english d5_ending_past_d4128fa7:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/06 ti.ogg"
    Pol "You're right. You're all I have left."


translate english d5_ending_past_bf0836e3:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/07 Ya.ogg"
    Pol "I believe you."


translate english d5_ending_past_a1bf20fb:


    "I looked over her shoulder. "


translate english d5_ending_past_d7bd46c4:


    "A black rectangular hole caught my eye at the end of the graveyard section."


translate english d5_ending_past_a0f6ebf9:


    "The wreath on the cross dangled its mourning stripes as if telling me to look inside."


translate english d5_ending_past_267b9bd9:


    "I hobbled toward the hungry hole in the frozen loam on stiff legs."


translate english d5_ending_past_b5ba076d:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/08 Ant.ogg"
    Pol "Anton?"


translate english d5_ending_past_bdb39e2d:


    "The hole was calling for me."


translate english d5_ending_past_c47e00be:


    "I stepped over the short fence."


translate english d5_ending_past_34dc542b:


    "Snowflakes swirled in the air like royalty in a ballroom."


translate english d5_ending_past_dcf77145:


    "Six feet under the ground, covered by a powdery film of snow, lay my parents."


translate english d5_ending_past_de3fd621:


    "Hugging each other like in bed, but on the cold ground."


translate english d5_ending_past_1a0e5f21:


    "Their heads were turned toward each other as if parodying an intimate moment, and their temples were adorned by perfectly round bullet holes."


translate english d5_ending_past_e1e1b135:


    "Lumps of lead made Mom and Dad make up forever in death—it stifled the flames of their worthless squabbles."


translate english d5_ending_past_48f4d99c:


    "I fell to my knees, losing the last bits of sanity and strength."


translate english d5_ending_past_a3610189:


    Ant "No! This can't be true! This is all a lie!"


translate english d5_ending_past_dc3502c7:


    "Polina got closer."


translate english d5_ending_past_0a0132f2:


    "Her pupils shone in the dark."


translate english d5_ending_past_f8cb181a:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/09 mi.ogg"
    Pol "We'll be fine."


translate english d5_ending_past_96e76224:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/222.Etot.ogg"
    Ant "This nightmare..."


translate english d5_ending_past_330765da:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/222.On.ogg"
    Ant "It won't let us go."


translate english d5_ending_past_e78eb2b3:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/10 ti.ogg"
    Pol "Have you forgotten, silly?"


translate english d5_ending_past_74c56822:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/11 poka.ogg" 
    Pol "You're safe as long as you're with me."


translate english d5_ending_past_47b387ed:


    "Her right eye burst out."


translate english d5_ending_past_a88ff4ee:


    "Bits of her brain and bone marrow burst out of the eye socket, splashing on my horrified, twisted face."


translate english d5_ending_past_ef31e970:


    "Polina collapsed near a leaning gravestone. I rushed to her side."


translate english d5_ending_past_eb7dbb0b:


    "I touched her once beautiful but now disfigured face."


translate english d5_ending_past_0b41520e:


    "Gray smoke rose out of her eye socket."


translate english d5_ending_past_ea024fd2:


    "I felt the music leave her body that was quickly losing its warmth."


translate english d5_ending_past_3d5e048e:


    "My nostrils picked up the aroma of her hair, the smell of coniferous needles and firecrackers."


translate english d5_ending_past_5ec3e1e1:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/224.Poli.ogg"
    Ant "Please, don't abandon me, Polina!"


translate english d5_ending_past_d6c7ebd6:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/224.Polina.ogg"
    Ant "Polinaaaaaa!"


translate english d5_ending_past_4b152f50:


    "The barrel of a jet black gun got pressed against my forehead."


translate english d5_ending_past_265b2191:


    "Click."


translate english d5_ending_past_265b2191_1:


    "Click."


translate english d5_ending_past_1ceca1b4:


    "The man with a harelip fiddled with the gun in his hand."


translate english d5_ending_past_f906c4d8:



    voice "voice/killer/01Nado.ogg"
    Killer "Dang. Ran out of ammo."


translate english d5_ending_past_aadb8b21:


    "It almost felt like he was waiting for me to sympathize with him."


translate english d5_ending_past_ad3b4f89:



    voice "voice/killer/02Vot.ogg"
    Killer "Fuck my life..."


translate english d5_ending_past_4f67b963:


    "The killer shoved his gun behind his belt."


translate english d5_ending_past_0a0504df:


    "He looked up at the sparkling stars. Then, he slowly crossed himself."


translate english d5_ending_past_3d6f8d0e:



    voice "voice/killer/04 Gospa.ogg"
    Killer "God have mercy on me..."


translate english d5_ending_past_4304829c:


    "His merciless hands shoved me into the snow pile and gripped my neck."


translate english d5_ending_past_fae21c90:


    "The man with a harelip scowled."


translate english d5_ending_past_aea79266:


    "Then squeezed."


translate english d5_ending_past_3d7133e6:



    voice "voice/killer/08prosty.ogg"
    Killer "According to your unfailing love, according to your great compassion, blot out my transgressions."


translate english d5_ending_past_12420536:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/225.Udu.ogg"
    "His fingers clutched my neck, preventing me from breathing. His nails tore into my skin."


translate english d5_ending_past_32185cd4:


    "I dangled my heels, and the world around me started its danse macabre. I saw double, no, triple the crosses."


translate english d5_ending_past_b1677bed:


    "My pants became wet and hot."


translate english d5_ending_past_7ea05686:


    "Blue circles that looked like rainbow stains that gasoline left in puddles, spread before my eyes."


translate english d5_ending_past_3c3566aa:


    voice "voice/killer/10e.ogg"


translate english d5_ending_past_76ab455b:


    Killer "And grant your grace to the souls of the departed little ones..."


translate english d5_ending_past_0b1ead32:


    "I tried to remember Polina."


translate english d5_ending_past_d32dcfd7:


    "Majestic and beautiful."


translate english d5_ending_past_711c197c:


    "I imagined her playing on stage for thousands of people, with me sitting in the front row and never taking my eyes off her."


translate english d5_ending_past_6f7a5872:


    "I tried to remember Olya."


translate english d5_ending_past_e7a71c26:


    "I imagined carrying her, enveloped in sunlight, and us dissolving into the whiteness of first morning rays."


translate english d5_ending_past_d84cdddc:


    "A happy and peaceful feeling that was hitherto unknown to me took over my soul."


translate english d5_ending_past_3b7f49b1:


    "I felt calm, as if I just woke up from a nightmare, right in the middle of a pitch-black night, in my own room."


translate english d5_ending_past_6d945515:


    "Yes. This was all just a dream."


translate english d5_ending_past_b1cf25dc:


    "Just a trick my imagination played on me."


translate english d5_ending_past_e1cff15a:


    "And then I once again fell into pleasant slumber, happy that none of this was actually happening to me."


translate english d5_ending_past_58969e2e:


    "When the morning comes, I'll see my little sister, my parents, Polina, my friends..."


translate english d5_ending_past_29bc4a6b:


    "But no matter how much I tried..."


translate english d5_ending_past_7f92df59:


    "...I could no longer wake up."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_8c909c11:


    "I had to drag my little sister out of the car. She sniffled and shook like a paper doll in my embrace."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_914480ed:


    "The four of us rushed through the white haze on the snaking graveyard trail."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_4278f651:


    "It felt like those hungry monsters could pounce at us at every moment."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_f1e1f8f3:


    "Shadows of the crosses overlapped on the trail."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_6dbce6b9:


    "A deafening howl echoed from behind us."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_4d6c9e27:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/223 R.ogg" 
    Pol "Roma!"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_0272f77b:


    "I turned around. Polina was alone."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_ce58bf0e:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/210.Gde.ogg"
    Ant "Where is he?"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_9f14459b:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/224 to.ogg" 
    Pol "He was holding my hand a moment ago! Roma!"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_1cb4ab10:


    "My gaze stumbled upon the leather coat, dangling on one of the crosses."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_e8cf35f3:


    "Romka's coat."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_b7de8d0e:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/211.Poshle.ogg"
    Ant "Let's go, Polina. Try to keep up."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_ad58cae7:



    voice "voice/Polina/5day/225 a.ogg" 
    Pol "What about Roma?"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_60dd18a9:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/212.on.ogg"
    Ant "He'll catch up to us. Give me your hand."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_103402d1:


    "But Polina didn't listen. She took a step back, then another one, shouting Romka's name into the nonresponsive darkness."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_651088f1:


    "Her voice, hoarse and trembling, dissolved in the blizzard like an unsuccessful spell."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_48d11fc6:


    "The only reply she got was a low, guttural howl, followed by a short burst of gunshots."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_2c7d1ecd:


    "A sudden gust of snow devoured the girl's figure. Polina disappeared inside it without a trace. No screams, no shadow. Just an empty void."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_a727c216:


    "I couldn't help her. I needed to protect my sister."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_a7342467:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/226.S.ogg"
    Ant "Come on, let's go."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_4aec438f:


    "We walked like two runaway kids in their search for the Neverland who got lost and ended up in the frozen wastelands of the Snow Queen."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_fc1627ff:



    voice "voice/olya/5day/123 Ti.ogg"
    Oly "Will you always stay with me?"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_6d074693:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/227.Ni.ogg"
    Ant "Of course."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_997f65bf:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/228.No.ogg"
    Ant "But, Olya..."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_d9a5218d:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/229.Es.ogg"
    Ant "If something does happen to me, run away, okay?"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_df7c416a:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/229.Eshi.ogg"
    Ant "Look for adults, for our parents..."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_29cb9a43:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/230.Ko.ogg"
    Ant "Look for anyone who's not wearing a mask."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_df9768a8:



    voice "voice/olya/5day/124 Dav.ogg"
    Oly "Let's do something so nothing happens."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_cc457aeb:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/231.ko.ogg"
    Ant "Sure, but..."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_71e13897:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/231.po.ogg"
    Ant "Promise me you'll run for help if..."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_b7e583b9:



    voice "voice/anton/5day/232.Es.ogg"
    Ant "If I won't be able to walk anymore."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_91bd382b:



    voice "voice/olya/5day/125 Kl.ogg"
    Oly "I swear on Mom's heart!"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_4d4f6686:


    "Despair made me want to howl along with the wind."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_d7bd46c4:


    "A black rectangular hole caught my eye at the end of the graveyard section."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_a0f6ebf9:


    "The wreath on the cross dangled its mourning stripes as if telling me to look inside."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_267b9bd9:


    "I hobbled toward the hungry hole in the frozen loam on stiff legs."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_e4008983:



    voice "voice/olya/5day/126 To.ogg"
    Oly "Where are you going, Tosha?"


translate english d5_ending_hunt_bdb39e2d:


    "The hole was calling for me."


translate english d5_ending_hunt_c47e00be:


    "I stepped over the short fence."


